WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.650
In a fertility clinic
freezer sit spare embryos,

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.980
each about 5 days old.

3
00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.560
They were made for fertility
treatment, then never used.

4
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:14.830
Their cells may one day help treat
diseases such as Parkinson's or diabetes.

5
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.020
But taking the cells destroys the embryo.

6
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:22.330
So can a few cells in a
dish be used to save lives?

7
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.810
In this mission, you'll read what the Torah
and the rabbis teach about life before

8
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.800
birth.

9
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:33.640
Then you'll weigh up whether the duty to
save life can justify research on embryos.

10
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.610
Your mission: weigh up whether cells
in a dish may be used to save lives.
